{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/400028-gmc-pledges","id":400028,"title":"GMC Pledges","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-09T23:05:25-08:00","id":400028,"title":"GMC Pledges","content":"I know we will get <b>Changeling</b> 2ed but it's still some months to this day. For now, what do you think should be changes in Plegdes system in vain to the <b>Demon</b>'s Pacts? Just rip-off <b>DtD</b> mechanics and paste them over the Wyrd/Tru Name/Divine connection of changelings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T23:17:14-08:00","id":400048,"title":"","content":"No, not least because <i>it's the entire conceptual basis of their powerset and it traditionally works on an entirely different medium.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T23:40:28-08:00","id":400078,"title":"","content":"But the Boons of Pledges could work with the <b>Demon</b>'s Pact system nicley.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T23:42:15-08:00","id":400079,"title":"","content":"Here's what I said the last time this sort of thing came up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think understanding the differences between the two can be used to sharpen <i>Changeling</i>, which is showing some of it's problems over the years. That said, <b><i>Demon can't answer Changeling's problems</i></b>, it can only <i><b>inform</b> </i>their solution. <i>Changeling</i> problems needs <i>Changeling </i>answers, because <i>Changeling </i>is not <i>Demon</i>. </div> </div> </div>I have not shifted from that position, and hell if I have to explain in depth why it doesn't work.<br /> <br /> Hell, I think I already did in the referenced source.<br /> <br /> EDIT: In fact, I did, somewhat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But a certain point of it must remain, and that comes back to our good old buddy, the source inspirations. With that in mind, it becomes clear why the limited benefits of <i>Demon</i> doesn't fly with <i>Changeling</i>.<br /> <br /> See, categorically, fae and demons have traditionally asked for very different things. The demonic tends towards what Descent goes for-they largely ask for the service of a person, or for some aspect of their life, or of course they ask for the soul. The things they give seem different from what they take by contrast. This often goes back to the unholy purposes of demons and the scale they work at-in the end, only the souls of the people they deal with ultimately matter. THe limitations are aesthetically and thematically in line for demon.<br /> <br /> But in faerie tales? Fae ask for weird stuff all the time, in ways that seem similar, but ultimately they seek to benefit as much as the characters, and they have much more in common-granted, what they take from people tends to stir their life as much as a demon's pledge does, but the benefits the fae receives is equal to what the other side can receive as well. It's true to form for <i>Changeling</i> to do so too.<br /> <br /> There's also a little notation in regards both styles in a mathematical sense: the fae are about proportionate trades, the demons are about improportionate trades. In faerie tales, what is given is often equal to what is taken( least within it's own context), and it makes sense that if the fae were denied options to receive that the other had, it would cease to be 'equal' and 'fair'. All options must be on the table, all must equal zero-that is the way of the fae.<br /> <br /> By contrast, demons often try to get people to think that what they are getting is worth more than it really is, exacting large payments for minor things. This makes sense, they are liars, cheaters, manipulators. Things are not equal. It seems appropriate, then, that they do get shafted on what's available to them-they only have access to what's important to them, and the people they deal with only get what's important to them. The entire nature of pacts is unfair to all, it is openly unequal. The entire affair is slanted and askew, and the center cannot hold. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T23:54:13-08:00","id":400092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/400028-gmc-pledges?p=400078#post400078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Boons of Pledges could work with the <b>Demon</b>'s Pact system nicley.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could also work with the system presented in <i>Summoners</i>, which at least has the benefit of not being confined to a <i>literal written document</i> in a context where half the problem of the fae is <i>watching what you say so that you aren't held to a promise you never meant to make.</i><br /> <br /> But the pledge system is not going to benefit from porting other games' dealing systems directly, because unlike those things the word-bond is a central aspect of the game's metaphysics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T23:56:31-08:00","id":400094,"title":"","content":"Learn from past travels, but don't walk the same roads.<br /> <br /> Man, there's Changeling in quite a nutshell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T11:38:41-08:00","id":402187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/400028-gmc-pledges?p=400092#post400092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It could also work with the system presented in <i>Summoners</i>, which at least has the benefit of not being confined to a <i>literal written document</i> in a context where half the problem of the fae is <i>watching what you say so that you aren't held to a promise you never meant to make.</i><br /> <br /> But the pledge system is not going to benefit from porting other games' dealing systems directly, because unlike those things the word-bond is a central aspect of the game's metaphysics.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true but since the other pact systems are just variations of the original Changeling system just augmented to suit those games I don't see Pledges changing. Personally, obviously at this point, I wish they would. The problem with the pact system is that it's hard to make something that you essentially mechanically game for the best Pros and the least cons, into something more than just a tool. It'd take a real pro to make the system be more than just a bunch of free dots and tasks. I don't mean from a story perspective I mean from an out of game perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-11-2015, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T13:18:51-08:00","id":402320,"title":"","content":"David's mentioned that he has ideas on how to fix pledges, so it's probably changing to some extent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}